<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Draw First Point</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from the</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>tree context menu</b></span> <span class="Path">for</span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>polylines &gt; Draw First Point</b></span></i><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span></b> <span class="Command">Draw First Point</span> <span lang="EN-GB">is available for polylines only. If you enable it, the first node of every polyline will be visualised as yellow filled square. This square is larger than the points, squares, and crosses that are used for displaying nodes.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command affects to all polyline groups in the active window although it was applied to a single polyline or polyline group. The other open windows are not influenced on it. The state of</span> <span class="Command">Draw First Point</span> <span lang="EN-GB">is not stored, i.e. next time when you open the file first points will not be displayed.</span></p>
<p class="Use"><span lang="EN-GB">This command is</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>useful</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">when preparing section data for export to a CAD system or when preparing to combine polylines. It is better to see what is the direction of polylines before reversing it or sort polylines.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></p>
